From fc4f2a55ff99f2183541876e183f7ffd9646dfd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Devaney <patrickbdevaney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:58:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek41 : two-level candidate-block mask, lift the 16384
 clamp when present

The reference (model.py Indexer.forward, select_candidate_blocks) has the candidate source
layer (20) score its compressed rows as usual, take the best row of every block of 8, pin the
block holding the query's newest row, and keep the top 2048 blocks. Every later index source
(24, 28, 32, 36) masks its own indexer score to those blocks before its top-k; the layers in
between reuse that top-k (patch 0002). The source itself is not restricted. Past 2048 x 8
compressed rows this tree attended outside the picked blocks and silently diverged.

- src/models/deepseek41-candidates.h: the mask as a ggml subgraph from existing ops only
  (pool_1d max, exp/pad/sub for the pin, top_k, fill + set_rows, broadcast add); no new op,
  every op already has a CUDA kernel. While n_blocks <= topk_blocks every reachable block is
  kept, so nothing is built and the graph is exactly the old one.
- deepseek41.cpp: build at the candidate source, apply at later index sources, prefill and
  decode alike (per-query n_visible from the plan's causal mask).
- Optional KVs deepseek41.candidate.{source_layer,topk_blocks,block_size}, written by the
  converter from config.json and checked at load (source must be an index source; later index
  sources must share its ratio; block size must divide the 256-row plan padding).
- llama-context: the 0006 clamp now applies only to a file without those keys. Older files can
  pass them with --override-kv; LLAMA_DSV41_UNSAFE_LONG_CTX keeps its meaning there and is
  ignored when the mask is present.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FRxsM9A6MEwiwPjBPC6hDa
